ario  Kart littlebigplanet karting Strax make  you feel like you've been shrunk down  into an arts and crafts project with  cardboard cutouts stickers and sushi  rolls instead of tires it's a stupidly  adorable coat of paint on a kart racer  it still features all the mechanics  you're used to plus some grappling hook  action for Indiana jonesing / pits just  like littlebigplanet creativity is what  really sets this kart racer apart you  can create your own tracks and then  upload them for other people to try the  creativity doesn't stop there you can  also modify game rules create weapons  and more even though there's a pretty  steep learning curve to the editor  lastly littlebigplanet karting boasts  would mario kart 8 sort of left out  proper battle arenas you don't have  three little balloons floating over your  head but there are specially designed  ballerinas so you and your friends can  blow each other's heads off while it's  still being adorable  licensed games are usually just they  recreate whatever movie they're based on  in a crappy platformer or adventure game  for children so stay with me on this one  because cars to the game is actually  great a little bit Mario Kart a little  bit split second this isn't a story game  it's a racer along with the cart  mechanics and use of weapons you're  familiar with you have a jump button and  can perform flips spins and two wheel  driving tricks to fill up your boost bar  another trick throw your car in reverse  which can be used as a strategy to shoot  the cars behind you even though it is  cars themed with cars cutscenes and cars  voices the racing feels less skittish  instead of silly carts you have sleek  cars instead of banana peels and red  shells you have oil slicks on  side-mounted machine guns instead of  racing on high fantasy tracks you race  in locations like Tokyo London and  Monaco yes that Monaco track not to  mention some of the game modes are  straight from our FPS in hunter you  encounter waves of 